invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: both_powers returns after the exponentiations on AVX-512 IFMA
  without wiping the vector and mask registers, which hold digits of the
  primes and of their tables' entries until other code writes them. The
  signature is the same. bin/x86_kernels_test counts the calls into
  avx512_wipe_registers on test/rsa_ifma_sign_count.c's stand-in and
  requires two from each signature on the kernels. Only an x86-64 object
  makes the call, so test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds the binary for
  x86-64; the lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded
  rather than caught.

--- old
        rsa_ifma_sign_power_pair(m1, m1, k->dp, mod_p, m2, m2, k->dq, mod_q, half_len);
        rsa_ifma_sign_wipe_below();
        wipe_vector_registers();
--- new
        rsa_ifma_sign_power_pair(m1, m1, k->dp, mod_p, m2, m2, k->dq, mod_q, half_len);
        rsa_ifma_sign_wipe_below();
